From 048a3ba31c395c1e4b0779385151616110e44095 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:25:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 46/46] media: qcom: iris: adapt the SM8450/SM8475 VPU2 support
 to Linux 7.3

Linux 7.3 gained encoder key-frame requests (upstream 6f62dcefd249,
"media: qcom: iris: Add request key frame support for encoder") and
split the platform firmware descriptor into firmware_desc_gen1/gen2.
The cherry-picked VPU2 support (93acb52146de, from linux-marble
af1b85e54f57) carried its own copy of the former and used the old
single descriptor.

Drop the duplicate HFI_PROP_REQUEST_SYNC_FRAME definitions, the
REQUEST_I_FRAME capability and its iris_set_req_sync_frame_gen2()
setter in favour of the upstream REQUEST_SYNC_FRAME capability that
SM8550 encoder caps (shared by VPU2) already carry, and describe the
SM8450 HFI gen2 firmware with firmware_desc_gen2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
